# The dataset tree is a build artefact whose bytes are part of the contract:
# `build-ds2.ts --check` re-emits it and compares byte for byte, and each sample
# pins its upstream blob. CRLF conversion on checkout would break both, so the
# dataset keeps the exact bytes git stores.
datasets/self-built/** -text

# The provenance registry's anchors are sha256 of the file on disk, so the bytes
# under `artifacts/acceptance/` are part of the contract too: on a machine with
# `core.autocrlf=true`, a fresh checkout would turn them CRLF and every
# `sha256:` row would stop recomputing. The gate would go red rather than pass
# silently, but a registry that only verifies on one machine is not a registry.
artifacts/acceptance/** -text
